comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:26:12.086Z",codex-agent,"Design: approved public emails, not display names; audit author and committer on every reachable commit after the root anchor. Read controls from the trusted default branch after adoption so a PR cannot widen its own allow-list or advance its own baseline. Keep the existing tracked UTF-8 path gate and the release hold."
  "2026-10-17T09:28:15.594Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: replacing only scripts/identity.ts with origin/main leaves the new tests unchanged and fails 6 of 7 cases, including approved fleet identities and missing-base refusal. Restoring the implementation passes 7 of 7. Typecheck and docstring gates pass. No tags, publishing or release activation."
  "2026-10-17T09:31:57.200Z",codex-agent,"Validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed in CI identity environments. Each ran 47 tests with 47 passes, zero failures or skips; all source statements, branches, functions and lines are 100%. Both packed npm and Bun consumer acceptances passed. Linked adversarial tests also passed 7/7. The root anchor covers every later kit and merge commit. Release remains held."
